  id: Cervicoscutular_muscle.L
  partName: Cervicoscutular_muscle.L
  descriptionChunks:
  - The cervicoscutular muscle is a thin, superficial muscle that primarily assists
    in moving the skin over the neck and shoulder region. It also contributes to
    minor shoulder movements and plays a role in subtle adjustments of body positioning.
  - ' Although not a major force-generating muscle, it is important for fine motor
    control and flexibility. It helps maintain skin tension and supports coordinated
    movement between the neck and upper limb structures.'
